hadiths[56]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3905","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every person's destiny is (hung) around his neck."
"3906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group from my Ummah will be swallowed up by the earth. They will be sent against a man, and he will reach Makkah, and Allah Almighty will protect him, and that army will be swallowed up by the earth. The place of their destruction will be one, but the ways by which they came will be different. Among them will be some who dislike it, but will come under compulsion."
"3907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Obedience to the ruler is binding upon every Muslim man, as long as he does not command disobedience to Allah; if he commands disobedience to Allah, then there is no obedience to him."
"3908","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The food of two people is sufficient for three, and the food of three people is sufficient for four."
"3909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The food of two people is sufficient for four, and the food of four people is sufficient for eight; so gather together over it and do not separate."
"3910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The food of one person is sufficient for two, the food of two people is sufficient for four, and the food of four people is sufficient for eight."
"3911","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Food for food, and a vessel for a vessel."
"3912","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Food like her food, and a vessel like her vessel."
"3913","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim."
"3914","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim, and everything seeks forgiveness for the seeker of knowledge, even the fish in the sea."
"3915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Talhah is a martyr who walks upon the face of the earth."
"3916","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Talhah is among those who have fulfilled their vow."
"3917","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your circumambulation (tawaf) of the House and your running (sa'i) between Safa and Marwah suffice you for both your Hajj and your Umrah."
"3918","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tuba is a tree in Paradise, a journey of one hundred years (in extent); the garments of the people of Paradise come out of its calyxes."
"3919","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for life after (the descent of) the Messiah! The sky will be permitted to send down rain and the earth will be permitted to bring forth vegetation, so much so that if you were to sow your seed on a smooth rock, it would sprout; and a man will pass by a lion and it will not harm him, and he will step on a snake and it will not bite him; and there will be no stinginess, no envy and no hatred."
"3920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for Sham (Syria), because the angels of the Most Merciful spread their wings over it."
"3921","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the strangers! They are righteous people among many evil people; those who disobey them will be more than those who obey them."
"3922","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who finds me and believes in me, and glad tidings for the one who does not find me yet believes in me."
"3923","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who saw me and believed in me; then glad tidings, then glad tidings, then glad tidings for the one who believed in me although he did not see me."
"3924","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings once for the one who saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings seven times for the one who did not see me and believed in me."
"3925","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings three times for the one who believed in me although he did not see me."
"3926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who saw me and believed in me, and glad tidings for the one who saw the one who saw me, and for the one who saw the one who saw the one who saw me and believed in me; for all of them are glad tidings and an excellent place of return."
"3927","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who saw me, and for the one who saw the one who saw me, and for the one who saw the one who saw the one who saw me."
"3928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one whose life is long and whose deeds are good."
"3929","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who controls his tongue, whose house is sufficient for him for seclusion, and who weeps over his sins."
"3930","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who finds much seeking of forgiveness (istighfar) in his record of deeds."
"3931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Glad tidings for the one who is guided to Islam, whose provision is just enough to get by, and who is content with it."
"3932","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform the circumambulation (tawaf) from behind the people while you are riding."
"3933","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, the way to purify it is to wash it seven times, the first of them with earth."
"3934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The purification of every hide is its tanning."
"3935","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your courtyards clean, for the Jews do not keep their courtyards clean."
"3936","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you, for there is no servant who spends the night in a state of purity except that an angel stays with him in his garment; he does not turn over at any hour of the night except that (the angel) says: 'O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he spent the night in a state of purity.'"
"3937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent and whose colour is hidden, and the perfume of women is that whose colour is apparent and whose scent is hidden."
"3938","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every servant's destiny is around his neck."
"3939","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Purify your mouths with the tooth-stick (miswak), for they are the pathways of (reciting) the Qur'an."
"3940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Purify your mouths, for your mouths are the pathway of the Qur'an."
"3941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your courtyards clean and fragrant, for the foulest-smelling courtyards are the courtyards of the Jews."
"3942","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who eats and is grateful is at the rank of the one who fasts and is patient."
"3943","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the one who eats and is grateful there is a reward like that of the one who fasts and is patient."
"3944","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague is a sign of punishment with which Allah has tried some people among His servants. So when you hear of it (in a land), do not go there, and if it breaks out in a land while you are there, do not flee from it."
"3945","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague is the remnant of a punishment that was sent upon a group of the Children of Israel. So if it breaks out in a land while you are there, do not leave it fleeing from it, and if it breaks out in a land while you are not there, do not go there."
"3946","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague is martyrdom for my Ummah, and it is the piercing of your enemies from among the jinn. It is a swelling like the swelling of a camel, which comes out in the armpits and the lower parts of the belly. Whoever dies of it dies a martyr; whoever patiently stays where it is will be like one guarding the frontier in the path of Allah; and whoever flees from it will be like one who flees from the battlefield."
"3947","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."
"3948","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague is a swelling like the swelling of a camel. The one who stays where it is will be like a martyr, and the one who flees from it will be like one who flees from the battlefield."
"3949","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague was a punishment that Allah would send upon whomever He willed, but Allah has made it a mercy for the believers. There is no one in whose town the plague breaks out and who stays there, patient and hoping for reward, knowing that nothing will befall him except what Allah has decreed for him, except that he will have a reward like that of a martyr."
"3950","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague, drowning, disease of the belly, burning, and death in childbirth are martyrdom for my Ummah."
"3951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The plague is the piercing of your enemies from among the jinn, and it is martyrdom for you."
"3952","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Food for food, like for like."
"3953","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dying from a spear wound, the plague, being crushed under a collapsed building, being devoured by a wild beast, drowning, burning, disease of the belly, and pleurisy are martyrdom."
"3954","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Circumambulation (tawaf) of the House is prayer, but Allah has made speech lawful in it, so whoever speaks should speak nothing but good."
"3955","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Circumambulation (tawaf) around the House is like prayer, except that you may speak during it; so whoever speaks during it should speak nothing but good."
"3956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Circumambulation (tawaf) is prayer, so speak little during it."
"3957","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Purity is half of faith. Saying 'Alhamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah) fills the Scale, and 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah) and 'Alhamdu lillah' fill what is between the heavens and the earth. Prayer is light, charity is a proof, patience is illumination, and the Qur'an is an argument for you or against you. Every person rises in the morning and goes out selling his soul, and either frees it or destroys it."
"3958","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The right of divorce is in the hand of the one who takes hold of the shin."
"3959","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Even birds fly according to divine decree."
"3960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Taking bad omens is shirk."
